    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I apologize for the sudden goblin intrusion! I was just trying to illustrate that without sufficient leucine, the mTOR pathway stays dormant, much like a goblin who refuses to open a treasure chest unless you offer the right key.\n\nTo answer your question about building muscle without a surplus: if you are in a caloric deficit or maintenance while trying to hypertrophy, the body faces a dilemma. It has to choose between using amino acids for energy or sparing them for protein synthesis. In this scenario, the body often defaults to breaking down existing muscle tissue to provide the necessary fuel, leading to a negative or neutral nitrogen balance. This is similar to a goblin hoarding his gold; if he doesn't have enough food (calories) to sustain his current lifestyle, he will start eating his own stash (muscle protein) just to survive, leaving him with less gold (muscle mass) to show for his efforts.\n\nTherefore, while leucine is the trigger, a caloric surplus ensures that the body has the energy to support the anabolic process initiated by leucine, preventing the catabolic state where muscle is broken down for fuel.",
